comments.body:
Ran this locally against master `c35d595` and the PR head `176f8aad` (.NET 8, `dotnet test` in `csharp/`):

- master: 83 passed, 1 skipped, 84 total.
- master + this PR's tests: `TestMultiSigPayloadSkipsMalformedEntry` fails with `Invalid Signature Headers` (the `throw` at `csharp/Svix/Webhook.cs:126`).
- this PR as submitted: 85 passed, 1 skipped, 86 total, matching the description.

To add to the cross-SDK note in the description: Ruby skips these too (`ruby/lib/svix/webhook.rb:54-55`).

Two small test suggestions, if useful:

1. A double space between entries hits the same path on master, because the empty token has no `,`. This fails on master with `Invalid Signature Headers` and passes with the PR:

```diff
+        [Fact]
+        public void TestMultiSigPayloadSkipsEmptyEntryFromDoubleSpace()
+        {
+            var testPayload = new TestPayload(DateTimeOffset.UtcNow);
+            var valid = testPayload.headers.Get(TestPayload.SVIX_SIGNATURE_HEADER_KEY);
+            testPayload.headers.Set(
+                TestPayload.SVIX_SIGNATURE_HEADER_KEY,
+                "v1,Ceo5qEr07ixe2NLpvHk3FH9bwy/WavXrAFQ/9tdO6mc=  " + valid
+            );
+
+            var wh = new Webhook(testPayload.secret);
+
+            wh.Verify(testPayload.payload, testPayload.headers);
+        }
```

2. `TestOnlyMalformedSignatureThrowsNoMatch` passes on master as written, since master throws the same exception type with a different message. Asserting the message makes it catch the change:

```diff
-            Assert.Throws<WebhookVerificationException>(() =>
+            var ex = Assert.Throws<WebhookVerificationException>(() =>
                 wh.Verify(testPayload.payload, testPayload.headers)
             );
+            Assert.Equal("No matching signature found", ex.Message);
```

With both added, all three new tests fail on master and pass with this PR, and the suite stays green (86 passed, 1 skipped, 87 total).

Written with AI assistance (Claude ran the repro and the tests and drafted this comment).
